   "text": "I read the molecule as a PROTAC-type compound: a 2-hydroxyphenyl aminopyridazine ligand, a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane, a pyrimidine, a cyclohexane linker, and a VHL-type tert-leucine/hydroxyproline ligand ending in a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamide.\n\n**Left to right:**\n- **Aryl pyridazine:** a 2-hydroxyphenyl is attached to a pyridazine. The pyridazine carries an NH2 and, next to it, the bicyclic nitrogen.\n- **Bicycle:** a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. N3 is bonded to the pyridazine and the bridging N8 is bonded to the pyrimidine.\n- **Pyrimidine:** it is 2,5-disubstituted. The 5-CH2 links to an N-methyl amine.\n- **Cyclohexane:** it is 1,4-disubstituted, with the N-methyl amine on one carbon and the carboxamide on the other. Both bonds are drawn as wedges, so I took the substituents as cis.\n- **tert-Leucine:** the carboxamide NH is attached to a tert-leucine unit, which I assigned as the (S) configuration drawn in the standard VHL ligand.\n- **Hydroxyproline:** the tert-leucine carbonyl is bonded to a 4-hydroxyproline nitrogen. The ring has a hashed OH and a wedged C2 carboxamide, which I took as the usual (2S,4R) arrangement.\n- **Benzylamide:** the proline carboxamide nitrogen carries a benzyl group, and the benzene bears a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\nI derived the cyclohexane and tert-leucine/proline chirality tags by hand from the drawn wedges and the standard VHL ligand, so the stereo tags are the least certain part.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc(N2CC3CCC(C2)N3-c2ncc(CN(C)[C@H]3CC[C@H](CC3)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)NCc3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)cn2)c(N)nn1"
